---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="INAES Regulatory Generator"
  subtitle="A desktop automation tool that converts spreadsheet data into strict fixed-width regulatory files with validation and integrity checks."
  eyebrow="Professional Tool · Case Study"
  stack={['Python', 'Tkinter', 'Excel', 'OpenPyXL', 'Validation', 'PyInstaller']}
>
  <div class="case-grid">
    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Problem</h2>
      <p>
        Regulatory submissions require rigid legacy TXT structures where headers, data records
        and trailers must satisfy exact field and byte-length requirements.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Solution</h2>
      <p>
        The desktop application starts from a controlled spreadsheet template, validates and
        normalizes the data, applies business rules and produces the required output files.
      </p>
    </article>

    <article class="case-panel">
      <h2>Integrity</h2>
      <p>
        The generated files are validated again at byte level to ensure each fixed-width record
        and total file size conform to the specification before delivery.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</CaseStudyLayout>
